 "rules": [
  "Scored on the held-out half of the frozen sample only (TOIs by sha256(seed:TIC) parity); the tuning half is never scored.",
  "A submission lists, for every star of its scope, the events its method detected on the real light curve and on the flux-inverted and block-scrambled controls (time, duration, period, its own pass verdict and flags). The leaderboard decides which events lie on the TOI's ephemeris (the benchmark's score_star and match_toi) and counts control false alarms itself. Self-reported outcomes are not accepted.",
  "Rank: Youden's J on the searchable set the benchmark fixed (stars with a SPOC 2-minute light curve), with one predicate on both sides, a clean candidate (on the ephemeris, passed, no eclipsing-binary flag): J = the share of CP/KP stars offered as clean candidates + the share of FP stars not offered − 1, with a square-and-add Wilson interval. Calling every TOI a planet, with or without a flag, scores J = 0; a searchable star called not searched counts as not offered. J over every star of the scope is shown beside it. Where intervals overlap, the order is not a measured difference.",
  "The controls gate ranking and do not enter J: only held-out entries with both control lists on every searched star are ranked, others are listed unranked. The control lists are the method's own report; the leaderboard cannot recompute them without the light curves. The Sentinel subsample is never ranked.",
  "A floor: the metadata-only baseline uses no light curve at all, only the public TOI number, period, duration, ephemeris errors and epoch, with a logistic regression fitted on the tuning half. A method that does not beat it is not shown to read the light curves better than the catalogue's own metadata predicts dispositions.",
  "A submission states the sha256 of the public inputs it was built from (tuning half with labels, held-out half without). Any other hash, tuned_on other than none or tuning, a field outside the whitelist, a missing or extra star, or missing provenance: refused, with the reasons listed.",
  "The hash is an attestation: the held-out labels are public in the repository, so the leaderboard cannot prove they were not read, and a method's pass verdicts and control events are its own report. Maintainer-held decoy light curves and prospective scoring on TOIs still undispositioned would close these gaps; neither exists yet.",
  "FP rejection: FP stars whose TOI dip the method did not offer as a clean candidate (recovered and not flagged). Reliability: the share of clean candidates on TOI dips that are CP/KP, on this sample's class mix, which is not the TOI catalogue's. All rates carry Wilson 95% intervals. TFOPWG dispositions are the reference, not ground truth for every TOI.",
  "Measured on a stated benchmark; nothing on this leaderboard is a discovery."
 ],
